ame><surname>Tsuang</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Mintz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Disability income, cocaine use, and repeated hospitalization among  schizophrenic cocaine abuser -- a government-sponsored revolving door?</article-title><source>NMAJ</source><year>1995</year><volume>333</volume><fpage>777</fpage><lpage>783</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7643886</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJM199509213331207</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riddell</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Riddell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Welfare Checks, Drug Consumption, and Health: Evidence from Vancouver Injection Drug Users</article-title><source>J Human Resources</source><year>2006</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>138</fpage><lpage>161</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Verheul</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Christenson</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mortality and morbidity associated with the distribution of monthly welfare payments</article-title><source>Acad Emerg Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>118</fpage><lpage>23</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9043538</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anis</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sun</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Guh</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Palepu</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schechter</surname><given-names>MT</given-n